# Dev tooling

## Scripts

| Script | Action |
|--------|--------|
| `yarn dev` | Vite dev server, port 3000 |
| `yarn build` | `clean` → `sync:static` → `tsc --noEmit` → `vite build` |
| `yarn clean` | removes `assets/` so stale hashed bundles do not accumulate |
| `yarn sync:static` | copies `src/public/fonts/*.woff2` to the shipped `fonts/` |
| `yarn check:contrast` | WCAG AA + sRGB gamut audit of the palette |
| `yarn verify` | typecheck + contrast |
| `yarn preview` | Serve the built output, port 4173 |
| `yarn typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |

## vite.config.ts

Exports a **function** of `({ command })`, not a plain object — `publicDir` differs
between dev and build.

- `root` is `src/`; `base` is `/`
- `build.outDir` is the repo root, `emptyOutDir: false` — see project-overview
- `publicDir` is `src/public` in dev, `false` in build. In production the out dir *is*
  the repo root, where `CNAME`, `favicon.ico` and `img/` already live; copying them over
  themselves is redundant and Vite warns when publicDir sits inside outDir.
  **`src/public/img/` must be kept in sync with `img/`** so dev and production resolve
  the same absolute paths.
- Every route is registered in `rollupOptions.input`. A new page that is not listed
  there will not be built.

## Yarn 4 has no pre/post scripts

**Yarn 4 does not automatically run `preX`/`postX` for custom script names.** A
`prebuild` script is silently ignored. Every step must be chained explicitly inside
`build`. This bit once: `prebuild` never ran, so `assets/` accumulated 54 stale bundles
and the self-hosted fonts were never copied into the build output — the deployed site
would have 404'd all four and fallen back to system stacks.

## Static files that ship

`img/`, `favicon.ico`, `CNAME` live permanently at the repo root. **`fonts/` is
generated** by `yarn sync:static` from `src/public/fonts/`, which is the source of
truth — edit fonts there, never in `fonts/`.

## Adding a page

Three steps, all required:

1. `src/<path>/index.html` — copy an existing one; update `<title>`, description, canonical
2. `src/entries/<name>.tsx` — `createRoot` mount
3. Register the HTML file in `rollupOptions.input`

## Dependencies

Runtime: `react`, `react-dom`, `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`, `class-variance-authority`,
`lucide-react`. Everything else is dev-only.

Do not add a router — routing is static HTML files by design (ADR-0002).
